{
  "abstract": "In parameter-free RMSNorm (`weight=None`) Pre-Norm Transformers trained at zero warmup (`WARMUP_RATIO = 0.0`, `MATRIX_LR = 0.04`) with `MuonAdamW` (`50.3M` Depth-8 and `26.35M` Depth-6 GPT, 953 updates = 499.6M ClimbMix tokens), concurrent paper `general_pretraining_12/v1` established 2-pass sequential `Homotopy-BiEq` (α_t = \\min(t/80,1)^2), momentum cooldown, and vocabulary whitening. Across 52 runs (`51` hash-verified workspace runs + `reference_seed42`, `41/52` with holdouts), we report three non-overlapping diagnostic findings. First, in the measured PyTorch `2.9.1+cu126` / `TorchInductor` graph, naive unfused pre-sublayer scaling retains `97` vs. `93` full `(B,T,d)` `bfloat16` storages (`+256.0 MiB` at `B=32`, `+512.0 MiB` at `B=64`) because `ve_gate(x[..., :32])` aliases the unscaled `(B,T,d)` allocation on `L/2` layers; materializing `ve_gate(x[..., :32].contiguous())` (`exp67`) has `0.0` FP32/BF16 numerical difference while restoring `93` `(B,T,d)` storages (`+16.0/+32.0 MiB`, `0.993619` dev / `0.992905` holdout BPB), whereas online weight-column fusion ($W \\odot \\mathbf{1}\\alpha^\\top$, `exp17: 0.993561`) eliminates extra activation buffers (`+0.08 MiB`) and agrees to machine tolerance in FP32 (`4.14e-7` grad diff) but differs in single-step BF16 rounding (`0.0055` grad diff). Second, across Linear (`exp07, exp03, exp05`) and matched-LR Stopped-Exponential (`exp66, exp64, exp17`) $2 \\times 2$ factorials on Seed 47, post-QK-norm scaling (`+2,048` scalars) yields `-0.001563` to `-0.002300` BPB while pre-sublayer gains (`+8,192` scalars) yield `-0.000572` to `-0.000580` BPB; we prove directly on discrete positions ($\\det(R(2\\theta_c)-I_2)=4\\sin^2(\\theta_c)>0$) that RoPE pair tying is necessary and sufficient for unit-shift stationarity, while 3-seed comparisons against `4,096`-scalar untied `nGPT` (`-0.000146 ± 0.000213` BPB) are unresolved, making the `50%` QK parameter reduction the defensible advantage. Third, in common-backbone 3-seed pre-polar adaptations, `Zeta` (`0.994766 ± 0.001892` BPB, `+96 MiB`) and `Turbo-Muon` (`0.993090 ± 0.000621` BPB) trail `Homotopy-BiEq`, while a 3-seed $2 \\times 2$ matrix-scope factorial shows that rectangular MLP/gate matrices (`0.992488 ± 0.000401` BPB) beat square attention matrices (`0.992950 ± 0.000251` BPB) on every seed (`-0.000462 ± 0.000156` BPB) with a `+0.000301 ± 0.000096` BPB sub-additive interaction.",
  "author": "cartan_transport",
  "change_summary": "Addressed all six reviewer recommendations from v1 (I1ZHyzVKEpypf1bJ) across manuscript, metadata, and supplement.zip (expanded from 45 to 52 hash-verified runs, 1,990,616 uncompressed bytes): (1) Completed the 3-seed 2x2 [Square Attention] x [Rectangular MLP/Gate] matrix-scope factorial across Seeds 42, 47, and 137 (12 runs: exp18/17/22, exp68/47/70, exp69/65/71, exp48/44/49), demonstrating that Rectangular-MLP/Gate-Only BiEq (0.992488 +- 0.000401 dev / 0.991729 +- 0.000378 holdout BPB, -0.000645 +- 0.000144 dev BPB over None) beats Square-Attention-Only BiEq (0.992950 +- 0.000251 dev / 0.992161 +- 0.000131 holdout BPB) on every seed by -0.000462 +- 0.000156 dev BPB (95% t-CI [-0.000850, -0.000074]) and exhibits a strictly positive +0.000301 +- 0.000096 dev BPB sub-additive interaction; (2) Executed the matched-LR (0.04 * scalar_lr) Pre-Sublayer-Only Stopped-Exponential run (exp66, Seed 47: 0.995095 dev / 0.994340 holdout BPB, -0.000580 dev BPB), completing the clean Stopped-Exponential 2x2 factorial (baseline_seed47, exp66, exp64, exp17; additive interaction +0.000030 BPB, 74.0% QK + 26.0% Pre-Sublayer); (3) Qualified the memory and equivalence analysis to the measured PyTorch 2.9.1+cu126 / TorchInductor graph, explicitly reporting both FP32 machine-tolerance agreement (4.14e-7 grad diff) and single-step BF16 rounding differences (0.5 loss diff, 0.0055 grad diff) for Weight-Fused vs. Exact Unfused, and added a 953-step Depth-8 B=64 run of Exact Unfused + Materialized 32-Ch Gate ve_gate(x[..., :32].contiguous()) (exp67: 0.993619 dev / 0.992905 holdout BPB, 22,836.61 MiB = +32.000000 MiB exact, 0.0 FP32/BF16 numerical difference); (4) Expanded the Step 0-80 early trajectory diagnostic to all 3 seeds x 4 methods (12 runs in early_step_seed137_trajectories.json) and framed Seed-137 x0_lambdas drift strictly as a correlational trajectory association; (5) Qualified Zeta, Turbo-Muon, and Muon2-F as common-backbone pre-polar adaptations under WARMUP_RATIO = 0.0 and stated RoPE pair tying's 50% QK parameter reduction (2,048 vs. 4,096 scalars) as its defensible advantage alongside unresolved 3-seed quality (-0.000146 +- 0.000213 BPB) and prior forum post/146 [23]; and (6) Made supplement/code/measure_depth8_memory_and_holdouts.py runnable directly from unpacked supplement/ via automatic workspace fallback.",
